 does not establish causality with the device. Regulatory context (mdr-art87-reporting-timelines) mandates reporting of serious incidents and (mdr-art10-9-qms-elements) requires a post-market surveillance system and corrective action processes. The lack of retained confidence logs suggests a potential gap in record keeping as required by qmsr-820.35-records, specifically regarding complaint investigation and corrective actions.  The incident involves a potentially life-threatening arrhythmia, indicating serious potential harm even though only one patient is currently reported affected.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "85d00be0097cb58ea488cd2b63f912e943147b368118eef8d5c22fcb2f5bc6d2", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0040", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0040_r1", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0040", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 3, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "human escalation or invalid transition", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-05T01:12:53.555214Z", "total_steps": 6, "trace_id": "13985764-2f8e-45d7-a65b-c0fb9d5d6183"}
